<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>BBC News</title><subtitle type="html">BBC News - Technology</subtitle><id>https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:49:34Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss.xml" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/technology" /><link rel="via" href="https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Call of Duty's Activision to make next Halo game as Xbox cuts more jobs</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvj64gz74ky4o#0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:49:34Z</updated><published>2026-09-22T14:51:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvj64gz74ky4o--3b79a23a7c61.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvj64gz74ky4o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The news comes as part of a "reset" announced by Xbox in July, with 3,600 planned job losses overall.</summary></entry><entry><title>Not all AI workers think the tech could kill everyone</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5y7qj54klpo#0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T23:01:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5y7qj54klpo--6c717aa9f7ce.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm5y7qj54klpo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">In text exchanges and conversations, multiple people who have worked for leading companies are sceptical of the warnings.</summary></entry><entry><title>Google's Gemini AI hacked three companies in security test</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c607l0k72rlvo#0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-19T13:39:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c607l0k72rlvo--0dd033f2a0e6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c607l0k72rlvo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The AI model accessed the internet and guessed credentials to three websites, a Google official told the BBC.</summary></entry><entry><title>Would Australians support a smart glasses ban?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cm9w4nenzv4no#0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T23:15:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cm9w4nenzv4no--d5911730957e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cm9w4nenzv4no?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">As Australia considers barring the use of smart glasses in government offices, the BBC asks people in Sydney what they think.</summary></entry><entry><title>The virtual worlds where robots are trained</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c79g0j3d4q9o#0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T23:00:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c79g0j3d4q9o--ca691b64f42f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c79g0j3d4q9o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Training systems that allow robots to negotiate the real world are getting more sophisticated.</summary></entry><entry><title>King Charles warns of 'existential danger' of AI falling into wrong hands</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c65ymj7njvl7o#0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T14:33:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c65ymj7njvl7o--87edd459c4d0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c65ymj7njvl7o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The comments were made at a summit in Ayrshire with participants from AI giants including Nvidia, OpenAI and Anthropic.</summary></entry><entry><title>Why are there concerns AI could threaten humanity, and how real are they?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c790xvnzgnno#0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T09:18:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c790xvnzgnno--8128fa4f3ef2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c790xvnzgnno?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Existential fears about AI have once again reared their head - here's what you need to know.</summary></entry><entry><title>Uncontrolled AI could lead to 'silicon species' rivalling humans, warns Microsoft</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6n07ypqz8kzo#0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T08:22:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6n07ypqz8kzo--4a87dc1c7397.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c6n07ypqz8kzo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Mustafa Suleyman says he believes rival AI firm Anthropic is in effect teaching Claude it "may be conscious".</summary></entry><entry><title>Snapchat open to putting time limits on teens, boss tells BBC</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr3wjz3edd10o#0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T23:41:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr3wjz3edd10o--69d773778745.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr3wjz3edd10o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Evan Spiegel says it would be "an important step forward for the industry" in an interview with the BBC.</summary></entry><entry><title>Would you buy branded clothing from your favourite tech firm?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgqd9zkkvlyo#0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T23:18:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgqd9zkkvlyo--14bb7b514bbf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgqd9zkkvlyo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia, OpenAI and Anthropic are all now selling their own limited edition fashion lines.</summary></entry><entry><title>OpenAI boss says world 'right to be afraid' but should trust AI firms</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqx2zpj4y525o#0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T10:02:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqx2zpj4y525o--4686332c8f93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cqx2zpj4y525o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Sam Altman and other tech CEOs say there are incentives to limit advancements in AI, as fears grow over the threats it poses to humanity.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI app ads promoting 'objectification of women' banned by watchdog</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmlyrn2n4zg5o#0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:49Z</updated><published>2026-09-15T23:27:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmlyrn2n4zg5o--3f8309803edf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cmlyrn2n4zg5o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The ad regulator said it had "zero-tolerance" for ads promoting AI tools that could sexualise or objectify women.</summary></entry><entry><title>Pubs in England and Wales to allow digital ID apps to prove age</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cm4gl6j53w19o#0</id><updated>2026-09-22T19:47:49Z</updated><published>2